{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"CVE-2009-20005","state":"PUBLISHED","summary":"A stack-based buffer overflow exists in the UtilConfigHome.csp endpoint of InterSystems Caché 2009.1. The vulnerability is triggered by sending a specially crafted HTTP GET request containing an oversized argument to…","description":"A stack-based buffer overflow exists in the UtilConfigHome.csp endpoint of InterSystems Caché 2009.1. The vulnerability is triggered by sending a specially crafted HTTP GET request containing an oversized argument to the .csp handler. Due to insufficient bounds checking, the input overflows a stack buffer, allowing an attacker to overwrite control structures and execute arbitrary code. It is unknown if this vulnerability was patched and an affected version range remains undefined.","published":"2025-09-16T14:32:00.691Z","lastModified":"2026-05-15T11:13:15.114Z","withdrawn":null,"severity":{"overall":"CRITICAL","cvss":9.3},"cvss":{"v2":null,"v3_0":null,"v3_1":null,"v4_0":{"vectorString":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","baseScore":9.3,"baseSeverity":"CRITICAL","exploitabilityScore":null,"impactScore":null,"source":"cve.org"}},"cwe":[{"cweId":"CWE-121","name":"CWE-121 Stack-based Buffer Overflow","source":"cve.org"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"InterSystems Corporation","product":"InterSystems Caché","cpe":null,"versions":[{"version":null,"status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"2009.1"}],"platforms":[]}],"configurations":[],"references":[{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework/master/modules/exploits/windows/http/intersystems_cache.rb","source":"cve.org","tags":["exploit"]},{"url":"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/16807","source":"cve.org","tags":["exploit"]},{"url":"https://www.juniper.net/us/en/threatlabs/ips-signatures/detail.APP:INTERSYSTEMS-CACHE-OF.html","source":"cve.org","tags":["third-party-advisory"]},{"url":"https://www.intersystems.com/products/cache/","source":"cve.