{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"CVE-2009-20006","state":"PUBLISHED","summary":"osCommerce versions up to and including 2.2 RC2a contain a vulnerability in its administrative file manager utility (admin/file_manager.php). The interface allows file uploads and edits without sufficient input valida…","description":"osCommerce versions up to and including 2.2 RC2a contain a vulnerability in its administrative file manager utility (admin/file_manager.php). The interface allows file uploads and edits without sufficient input validation or access control. An unauthenticated attacker can craft a POST request to upload a .php file containing arbitrary code, which is then executed by the server.","published":"2025-09-16T14:33:40.335Z","lastModified":"2026-05-15T11:13:15.916Z","withdrawn":null,"severity":{"overall":"CRITICAL","cvss":9.3},"cvss":{"v2":null,"v3_0":null,"v3_1":null,"v4_0":{"vectorString":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","baseScore":9.3,"baseSeverity":"CRITICAL","exploitabilityScore":null,"impactScore":null,"source":"cve.org"}},"cwe":[{"cweId":"CWE-434","name":"CWE-434 Unrestricted Upload of File with Dangerous Type","source":"cve.org"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"osCommerce","product":"osCommerce","cpe":null,"versions":[{"version":null,"status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"2.2 RC2a"}],"platforms":[]}],"configurations":[],"references":[{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework/master/modules/exploits/unix/webapp/oscommerce_filemanager.rb","source":"cve.org","tags":["exploit"]},{"url":"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/9556","source":"cve.org","tags":["exploit"]},{"url":"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/16899","source":"cve.org","tags":["exploit"]},{"url":"https://www.oscommerce.com/","source":"cve.org","tags":["product"]},{"url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/oscommerce-arbitrary-php-code-execution","source":"cve.org","tags":["third-party-advisory"]}],"exploit":null,"cred